# Coding Standards

- Kotlin 2.3, Compose Multiplatform 1.10, Material 3, Metro DI 0.9.1, Navigation 3
- Targets: Android, iOS, JS, WasmJS — all shared code in `commonMain`
- Classes ≤ 500 lines. Extract helpers, split large screens into sub-composables
- Use `DispatcherProvider` (injected), never raw `Dispatchers.IO`
- Use `@Inject` on the **class**, not the constructor
- Use `FleetLogger` for logging, never `println`
- Use `FleetDateTime` for date formatting, never manual string manipulation
- Colors from `MaterialTheme.colorScheme`, never hardcoded `Color(0xFF...)`
- Strings from compose resources `stringResource(Res.string.xxx)`, not hardcoded
- DTOs: `@Serializable` + `@SerialName("snake_case")` for API fields
- Domain entities: clean Kotlin data classes, no serialization annotations
- Never expose DTOs to presentation layer — always map to domain entities
- `Result<T>` from `ijs-error-lib` (Loading/Success/Error), not kotlin.Result
- Date format: API uses `DD-MM-YYYY` for costs/documents, `ISO 8601` for trips
